cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "arrangements: the category of arrangements, executable"
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Spivak
    given-names: David I.
repository-code: "https://github.com/dspivak/arrangements"
abstract: >-
  A library for building dynamical systems compositionally: components declare
  what they report forward and what they demand backward, and the dynamics of
  any interconnection is generated rather than derived by hand. The driving
  datum is a forcing one-form, which need not be exact, so one-way couplings
  such as sensors and controllers are native; the integrator is part of the
  arrangement, as a cotangent coalgebra, so there is a single dynamics functor.
keywords:
  - compositional dynamical systems
  - applied category theory
  - operads
  - retroactivity
  - gradient flow
license-url: "https://github.com/dspivak/arrangements/blob/main/LICENSE"
version: "0.1.0"
